{"step_index":164,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T15:00:33Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T17:00:33+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T17:00:33+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean`\nTotal Lines: 537\nTotal Bytes: 27292\nShowing lines 55 to 80\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n55:   unfold HasWitness; infer_instance\n56: \n57: /-- Greatest `k ≤ n` satisfying `p`, or `0` when none does. -/\n58: def maxUpTo (n : ℕ) (p : ℕ → Prop) [DecidablePred p] : ℕ :=\n59:   (((range (n + 1)).filter p).max).getD 0\n60: \n61: /-- Least `k ≤ n` satisfying `p`, or `n` when none does. -/\n62: def minUpTo (n : ℕ) (p : ℕ → Prop) [DecidablePred p] : ℕ :=\n63:   (((range (n + 1)).filter p).min).getD n\n64: \n65: /- ── order / size ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n66: \n67: def order (_G : SimpleGraph V) : ℕ := Fintype.card V\n68: \n69: def size (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ := G.edgeFinset.card\n70: \n71: /- ── independence / clique ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n72: \n73: /-- `s` is independent: no two of its vertices are adjacent. -/\n74: def IsIndependentFinset (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) : Prop :=\n75:   ∀ u ∈ s, ∀ w ∈ s, ¬ G.Adj u w\n76: \n77: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (s : Finset V) :\n78:     Decidable (IsIndependentFinset G s) := by\n79:   unfold IsIndependentFinset; infer_instance\n80: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":165,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T15:00:33Z","thinking":"**Examining definitions and dependencies**\n\nConsider `minUpTo`, `radius`, and `romanDominationNumber` definitions. `minUpTo` computes a minimum value up to a limit. `radius` calculates the minimum eccentricity. `romanDominationNumber` finds the minimum Roman domination weight, which relies on `IsRomanDominatingFunction`. Need to see the definition of `IsRomanDominatingFunction`.\n\n\n**Analyzing the target inequality**\n\n`IsRomanDominatingFunction G` requires that any vertex with value 0 has a neighbor with value 2.  `romanDominationNumber G` is the minimum Roman weight across all such functions. `radius G` is the minimum eccentricity of any vertex in G. The goal is to prove `radius G + 1 <= romanDominationNumber G`. It seems a direct proof may be viable, considering the relationship between the Roman domination and graph radius.\n\n\n**Testing the central inequality**\n\nHypothesis: For every Roman dominating function f, there exists a vertex v such that `ecc(v) + 1 <= weight(f)`. Testing on a path graph P6 with an optimal function (f(v2) = f(v5) = 2). Observation: v3 (a vertex with value zero) satisfies the inequality, but v2 (where f=2) does not.\n\nFurther test on cycle C6 where f(0) = f(3) = 2. It seems that the vertex that satisfies the inequality doesn't necessarily have a value of 2. It appears this may be dependent on the choice of Roman dominating function and its distribution of values across the graph. Need to verify that it works for *every* Roman dominating function.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c \"\n# Let's check what Lean knows about SimpleGraph in Mathlib\n# We can search Lean files in mathlib or use lean\n\"","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9","WaitMsBeforeAsync":1000,"toolAction":"Check mathlib","toolSummary":"Check mathlib"}}]}
